This C program initializes the GPIO and SPI interfaces on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to read moisture levels from a DFRobot Soil Moisture Sensor v2.0 using an MCP3008 ADC. It samples the sensor once per second, logging the raw 10-bit ADC value and a timestamp to the console. The program includes robust error handling for SPI initialization and transfer failures, ensuring that the SPI handle is closed and the driver library is terminated cleanly on all exit paths. It also supports graceful shutdown when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

