This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 to read sound pressure levels from two STMicroelectronics IMP23ABSU analog MEMS microphones using bit-banged I2C emulation on bus 1. It samples each microphone every 100 ms, computes the average level, and appends a timestamped entry of that average to a file named `audio_log.txt`. If a read from either sensor fails, it logs an error value of -999.0 dB for that sample and continues operation. The program also handles `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` by closing all I2C handles and terminating the driver cleanly.

