This code provides a complete solution for reading an analog voltage from a Honeywell MICROceL MCO-S4 CO sensor using an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 of a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It logs the voltage readings to a file named `co_log.txt` and controls an alarm connected to GPIO 4 based on the voltage threshold. The program handles errors, retries on SPI transfer failures, and cleans up resources on exit.

