This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B continuously monitors methane concentration using a Honeywell MICROpeL Model 41000-020 Combustible Gas Sensor interfaced through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI bus 0, channel 0. It reads the sensor once per second, logs each reading with an ISO-8601 timestamp to "methane_log.txt" in append mode, and writes a visible leak alarm to stderr whenever the concentration exceeds 1000 ppm. The program handles errors, logs any SPI transfer failure to stderr, and gracefully shuts down on SIGINT and SIGTERM.

