This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W continuously reads temperature and pressure data from a TDK ICP-10125 I2C sensor, logs each timestamped reading to a file named `environmental_data.csv`, and displays the values on the console for real-time monitoring. It handles graceful shutdown by catching `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`, closing both the I2C file descriptor and the CSV log file before exiting. The program checks the result of every I2C system call and retries after 5 seconds in case of sensor-absent or bus-error conditions.

