This code provides a complete solution for monitoring a potted plant using a HiLetgo Soil Moisture Sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC on the SPI bus of a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It logs the moisture percentage to a file every 60 seconds and sends an email alert if the moisture level falls below a specified threshold. The program handles initialization, error checking, and resource cleanup, and it gracefully handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

