This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W reads analog data from a SEN0193 Capacitive Soil Moisture Sensor using an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0. It configures the SPI interface and GPIO lines, reads the sensor data every 5 seconds, logs each reading with a timestamp, and handles sensor absence or wiring faults by checking for ADC values stuck at 0 or 1023. The program ensures that all resources are cleanly released on exit, including handling of SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

