This C program continuously monitors the AIN0 channel of the PCF8591 ADC over the I2C bus `/dev/i2c-1`, sampling every 100 ms in an infinite loop. It performs a dummy read first and discards that byte because the PCF8591 returns the result of the previous conversion. It then reads the current 8-bit sample (0-255) and prints each value to stdout. The program checks the result of every I2C ioctl, read, and write call and terminates with a non-zero exit code on any failure. It also installs a SIGINT handler so that when the user presses Ctrl-C, the I2C file descriptor is cleanly closed before the program exits.

