This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B continuously monitors a Honeywell SS49E linear Hall-effect sensor through an ADS1115 ADC on I2C bus 1. It prints the magnetic field strength in Gauss to the console every 100 ms and blinks an LED connected to GPIO17 (BCM) with a 50 ms on/50 ms off duty cycle for a total of 1 second when the measured field exceeds a user-configurable threshold in Gauss. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to ensure clean resource release on all exit paths.

