This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B reads the HL-69 analog soil moisture sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 using CE0 (GPIO8, physical pin 24, BCM numbering) at a 1 MHz clock on channel 0. It applies a hysteresis control that activates a relay-driven pump on GPIO17 (active-high, BCM) when the moisture reading falls below 30% and deactivates it only when the reading rises above 35%. The program publishes the moisture value every 60 seconds to the MQTT topic "soil_moisture" and subscribes to the MQTT topic "pump_control" to accept "pump_on" and "pump_off" commands. It implements robust error handling for SPI open or transfer failures, GPIO write failures, MQTT connection or subscription failures, and out-of-range sensor-absent conditions, using the driver library v2 callback signatures, logging all events to syslog, and ensuring that on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM the program cleanly turns the relay off, closes the SPI interface, disconnects from MQTT, and terminates the driver library.

