This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W reads the YL-69 soil moisture sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 using CE0 (GPIO8) at 1 MHz in SPI mode 0. It samples the ADC value from channel 0 (CH0) every 5 seconds, validates that the 10-bit result lies between 0 and 1023, converts it to a moisture percentage, logs each reading together with a timestamp to a file named `soil_data.txt`, implements a retry mechanism with exponential backoff on SPI read failures, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to perform a graceful shutdown.

