This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W reads the voltage from an MQ-3 alcohol sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 CE0 (GPIO8) using channel 0 in single-ended mode at 1 MHz, SPI mode 0 with 8-bit words. It samples the sensor once every second, classifies the reading into three ranges, and appends each timestamped measurement to a file named `alcohol_log.txt` using ISO 8601 UTC timestamps. The program robustly handles ADC read errors, detects a sensor-absent condition, and performs a graceful shutdown on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM.

