This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ continuously reads analog values from three single-ended MCP3008 channels (0, 1, and 2) over the SPI bus `/dev/spidev0.0` and logs the readings once per second to a CSV file named `sensor_data.csv`. The program checks the result of every open, ioctl, read, and write call and, on any failure, prints an error message and exits gracefully. It also installs a SIGINT handler so that when the user presses Ctrl+C, the CSV file is properly closed and the SPI resources are released before the program terminates.

