This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins. It continuously reads the digital output of a KY-038 sound sensor module connected to GPIO17 (BCM numbering) and prints the sound level reading (0 or 1) to the console each loop iteration with a 100 ms delay between reads. When the sensor reports a sound event (the DO pin goes LOW), it triggers an alarm LED attached to GPIO18 (BCM) by turning the LED on for 1 s and then off. The program handles initialization, error checking, and resource cleanup gracefully, including catching SIGINT (Ctrl-C) or SIGTERM and cleanly releasing all GPIO lines before exiting.

