This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B reads arrow-key presses and a 'q' character from stdin, uses the GPIO hardware PWM bus to drive two SG90 servo motors—one pan servo attached to GPIO17 (BCM) and one tilt servo attached to GPIO18 (BCM)—operating at a 50 Hz frequency. It initializes the libgpiod library, starts both servos at a neutral 90-degree position, moves each servo in 5-degree steps in response to the appropriate arrow key while enforcing angle limits of 0 to 180 degrees, inserts a 100 ms delay between successive commands, and handles cleanup by setting both servos to neutral, terminating the driver library cleanly, and exiting when a SIGINT signal is received or the user presses 'q'.

