This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W communicates with an Omron B5L-LD50-07050 3D TOF sensor over the I2C bus to detect intrusion events within 1 meter and log the average distance. The program sends the documented 4-byte command frame to request a measurement, waits at least 10 ms before reading the documented 15-byte response, verifies that byte 0 matches the documented header value, extracts the 16-bit big-endian distance from bytes 11 and 12, samples the sensor ten times per cycle with a 100 ms delay between cycles, computes the average distance, and when the average is less than 1000 mm, writes a timestamp and the average distance to a file named intrusion_log.txt. The program gracefully handles sensor-absent (I2C NACK) and bus-error conditions, and installs a SIGINT handler so that pressing Ctrl-C closes the I2C file descriptor and any open log files and releases all resources on every exit path.

