This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B opens the I2C bus 1 device file (`/dev/i2c-1`), sets the Melexis MLX75030 Time-of-Flight sensor as the I2C slave using `ioctl I2C_SLAVE`, and verifies that the device responds. It then enters a loop that every 500 ms reads the distance measurement from the sensor and prints a line to stdout in the form "Distance: <value> mm". If an I2C read fails, the program writes a diagnostic message to stderr and simply continues to the next cycle without exiting. If the sensor is not present at startup, it prints an error and exits with status 1. A SIGINT/SIGTERM handler is installed so that pressing Ctrl-C cleanly closes the I2C file descriptor and terminates the program with status 0.

