This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ uses the libgpiod library to implement an interrupt-driven parking sensor with an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor and a buzzer. The program initializes the GPIO pins, measures the distance, and continuously checks for sensor-absent conditions or invalid readings. It activates the buzzer while the measured distance is less than 30 cm and turns it off when the distance rises to 30 cm or more. The program ensures a clean shutdown on SIGINT.

