This code provides a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ that implements a proximity-based interactive art installation using an MPR121 capacitive touch sensor connected on the I2C bus. The program polls the touch status registers every 50 ms, monitors all twelve electrodes, and drives a distinct 4-bit LED pattern on GPIO 17, GPIO 18, GPIO 27, and GPIO 22 when any electrode detects proximity. It logs every proximity event to the console with a timestamp and handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions gracefully. The program ensures clean resource release on all exit paths by releasing all GPIO lines, closing the I2C and log file descriptors, and installing signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

