This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W uses the VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor on I2C bus 1 to poll distance measurements every 100 ms, converts the 16-bit register value from millimeters to centimeters, and controls a gate actuator connected to GPIO24 (BCM, active-high) based on the distance. The program logs each distance reading, each gate state change, and any errors with timestamps to a file named "gate_log.txt". It includes error handling for all I2C operations, sensor initialization, and file operations, and a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler that gracefully shuts down by closing the I2C interface, closing the log file, and terminating the driver library.

