This code provides a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W that interfaces with a Silicon Labs Si1102 proximity sensor on I2C bus 1, configures the sensor's proximity interrupt to GPIO27 (BCM numbering) on a rising edge, and on each interrupt reads the 16-bit proximity value, compares it to a threshold, and appends a line to a file named `proximity.log`. The program also accepts optional command-line options to set the I2C address and threshold, initializes the I2C interface and GPIO with full error checking, verifies every I2C transaction, GPIO setup, and file operation, and implements a thread-safe interrupt handler that does not perform blocking calls. The program installs a SIGINT handler that on receipt cleanly shuts down by closing the I2C device, closing the log file, and terminating the sensor driver.

