This code sets up an interrupt-driven system using the HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor and a buzzer on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins. The program measures the distance by generating a trigger pulse and measuring the echo pulse width, then prints the distance to stdout every second. It activates the buzzer if the distance is below 20 cm. The program handles errors, cleans up resources, and installs a SIGINT handler to ensure proper termination.

