This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B running a 64-bit kernel reads temperature and humidity from a Texas Instruments HDC1000 sensor attached via I2C on bus 1. It waits at least 20 ms after initiating a 14-bit temperature and humidity conversion before reading the result, logs the values to the console every 5 seconds, and handles errors such as sensor absence and read failures. It also installs handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to close the I2C file descriptor before exiting.

