This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the temperature from a Silicon Labs Si7051 temperature sensor connected via I2C on bus 1, with SDA on GPIO2 (BCM) and SCL on GPIO3 (BCM). The program logs the measured temperature in degrees Celsius to the console every 5 seconds. It handles I2C communication failures such as sensor absence, bus errors, and read/write timeouts, and ensures that all resources are cleanly released on every exit path, including a graceful shutdown when the process receives SIGINT or SIGTERM.

