This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B continuously reads the differential pressure from a Sensirion SDP800-500Pa sensor on the I2C bus. It waits at least 8 ms after each trigger before reading the three-byte response, verifies the CRC-8 for each measurement, and logs the timestamped pressure value to a file named `airflow_log.csv` with a header row added only when the file is newly created. The program includes error handling on every I2C call, detects and handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions, and ensures that all resources are cleanly released on normal termination as well as on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM.

