This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ continuously reads temperature from a Texas Instruments TMP117 high-accuracy temperature sensor on the I2C bus, sampling once per second and appending each reading to a file named `temperature_log.txt` using the exact format "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS, Temperature: <value> C\n". It checks the return value of every I2C call, handles both sensor-absent and bus-error conditions, attempts to re-initialize the I2C handle up to three consecutive times on failure before exiting, correctly processes negative temperature values, and ensures that on receipt of SIGINT (Ctrl+C) the program closes the I2C handle and terminates the driver cleanly on all exit paths.

