This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W continuously reads airflow data from a Honeywell HAF Series HAFUHH0025PA3 flow sensor over the I2C bus, sampling once every second. It extracts a 14-bit flow value and a 12-bit temperature value from a single 4-byte read using the sensor's API call. The program handles the first two reads after power-up which may return stale data, logs each timestamped measurement in SLPM and °C to a file named `flow_log.txt`, detects I2C communication failures, logs any read error, attempts to re-initialize the I2C handle, and cleans up resources on receipt of `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM`.

