This code provides a complete solution for driving a Sensirion SCD40 CO2 sensor over I2C on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B, including buffer management, error handling, and logging. The program uses the `libgpiod` library for I2C communication and `pthread` for threading. The main loop waits for one second after issuing the start-periodic-measurement command before the first read, then reads the sensor every five seconds, validating the CRC-8 of each value. The program logs any errors with timestamps to `/var/log/scd40_error.log` and persists the data to a timestamped CSV file in `/var/log/scd40_data/` with a header row. The program handles SIGINT by using a volatile sig_atomic_t running flag to stop the main loop, send the stop-periodic-measurement command, join the logging thread, flush any remaining buffered data to a final CSV file, close the I2C handle, and cleanly terminate the driver without any resource leaks.

