This code provides a complete implementation of a PID-controlled reflow oven using a MAX6675 thermocouple amplifier and a solid-state relay on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the temperature from the thermocouple at a 1 Hz rate, updates the SSR duty cycle based on the PID output, logs each temperature reading to a file, loads the target temperature profile from a file, handles robust error handling for SPI communication and GPIO control, and ensures that all resources are cleanly released on every exit path by handling termination signals.

