This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B continuously monitors a Bosch BMP280 pressure sensor on I2C-1, verifying the chip ID, applying compensation formulas, and logging pressure values exceeding 1020 hPa or falling below 980 hPa to a file named `pressure_log.txt` with timestamps. It handles I2C errors gracefully and ensures a clean shutdown on SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

