This C program for a Raspberry Pi 5 continuously monitors a YL-83 rain sensor connected to GPIO17 (active-low) via the GPIO bus. It polls the sensor every 2 seconds and, when rain is detected, commands an L298N motor driver to close a window by driving the motor forward for exactly 5 seconds using ENA on GPIO22, IN1 on GPIO23, and IN2 on GPIO24. Each detection, motor start, motor stop, and any error condition are logged to stdout with a timestamp. The program checks the return status of every driver call and explicitly handles the situation where the GPIO chip cannot be opened. It installs SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers to safely stop the motor and release all GPIO lines on program termination.

