This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W modulates a common-anode RGB LED connected to GPIO17, GPIO22, and GPIO27. It reads the CPU load from `/proc/stat`, maps the load to a color gradient, and sets the PWM values for each channel using the libgpiod library. The program handles initialization failures, installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and cleans up resources on exit.

