This code provides a complete solution for the Raspberry Pi Zero W to communicate with a BMP180 sensor on I2C bus 1, configure GPIO2 as a falling-edge interrupt with the internal pull-up enabled, and toggle data logging each time the interrupt occurs. The main loop polls at one-second intervals, reads the sensor using oversampling setting OSS=3, verifies that the calibration data is successfully read, obtains temperature in Celsius and pressure in Pascals, and appends a line to an altitude_log.txt CSV file containing the timestamp, temperature, and pressure. Every I2C read and write operation is checked for errors, and the program handles such errors gracefully. On receipt of SIGINT, it closes the I2C handle, closes the log file, and releases the GPIO before exiting.

