This code reads humidity and temperature from a DHT22 sensor connected to GPIO4 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the libgpiod library. It sends the measured values as a JSON payload to a specified API endpoint via HTTP. The program handles sensor absence, checksum mismatches, and network errors by retrying up to three times. It also ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including proper handling of SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

