This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W implements a PID controller to maintain a target temperature of 50°C by PWM-controlling a resistive heater on GPIO18. It reads the current temperature from a MAX31855 thermocouple amplifier connected on SPI0, logs every second to a file named `heater_log.txt`, and handles errors such as open-circuit, short-to-GND, or short-to-VCC conditions. The program also includes a failsafe that disables the heater if the reading exceeds 100°C or falls below 0°C. It cleans up resources on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM.

