This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ communicates over I2C bus 1 with an Analog Devices ADPD144RI red and infrared photometric sensor. It samples the sensor every 100 ms, logs each timestamped reading to a CSV file named `adpd144ri_log.txt`, and triggers an LED connected to GPIO17 whenever the infrared reading exceeds a threshold of 2000. The program robustly handles I2C errors and the case where the sensor is absent, and cleans up all resources—including the I2C bus, GPIO lines, and the log file—on every exit path, also handling `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` signals.

