This C program continuously monitors a SainSmart TTP223B capacitive touch sensor connected to GPIO 17 on a Raspberry Pi 5 using the libgpiod library. It polls the sensor every 100 ms and detects when the sensor remains continuously HIGH for more than 5 seconds, printing an intrusion alert to stdout. The program handles errors, cleans up resources on exit, and gracefully handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

