This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W continuously polls the digital output of a KY-026 Flame Sensor connected to GPIO20 (BCM) on the GPIO bus every 100 ms. It detects when the sensor state changes between flame detected and flame cleared, and appends a line to a file named `flame_log.txt` containing an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp and the new state only on each transition. The program verifies the success of every driver call and every file-I/O operation, explicitly handles the situation where the GPIO chip cannot be opened, and ensures that all resources are cleanly released on every exit path, including a graceful shutdown when the process receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM.

