This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B reads an 8-channel TTP226 capacitive touch sensor array connected via GPIO, polls the state of all channels every 50 ms, and writes to the console a CSV line for each poll containing an ISO-8601 timestamp followed by the eight channel states. It uses the libgpiod library for GPIO operations, checks every driver call for failure, handles the situation where the library cannot open the device or request any of the lines, installs a SIGINT handler so that pressing Ctrl-C triggers a graceful shutdown, and ensures that every line request and the chip resource are properly released on all exit paths.

