This C program initializes the libgpiod library to control the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It sets up the KY-033 Obstacle Avoidance Sensor Module connected to GPIO4 (BCM pin 7) as an input with an internal pull-up resistor. The program continuously polls the sensor every 50 ms, records each detection in a circular buffer of 100 entries, and prints an alert to stdout on every detection. When the program receives a SIGINT (e.g., from pressing Ctrl+C), it releases all driver resources, dumps the entire buffer in chronological order with human-readable timestamps, and exits cleanly.

