This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It continuously monitors two IR obstacle sensors connected to GPIO17 and GPIO18. The program checks if both sensors read LOW (0) continuously for at least 2 seconds, which is considered a stall. When a stall is detected, it records a timestamped entry in a file named `stall_log.txt`. The program handles signals to ensure clean resource release and avoids duplicate entries for the same stall event.

