This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W runs as a daemon and continuously polls the SEN0193 Water Level Sensor connected to GPIO23 (BCM numbering). It reads the sensor every 2 seconds and generates an alert whenever a logic HIGH is detected. The program logs alert messages to stdout and appends them to a file named `flood_log.txt` in the format "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS ALERT: Water detected". It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to release all resources cleanly before exiting. If a GPIO read fails, the program logs an error entry to the same file and schedules an automatic re-initialization attempt after 60 seconds.

