This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W continuously monitors the structural integrity of a miniature bridge model using two digital tilt sensors (Omron D7E-3) connected to the GPIO bus. It logs ISO-8601 timestamps to a file named `bridge_integrity.log` for tilt-start, threshold-exceeded, and tilt-end events. The program activates an alarm (buzzer/LED) if either sensor reads HIGH continuously for more than 2 seconds and deactivates the alarm when both sensors return to LOW. It includes error handling, clean shutdown handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and ensures the alarm is off on all exit paths.

