This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 5. It reads data from four infrared obstacle avoidance sensors connected to GPIO pins 4, 17, 27, and 22 (BCM numbering) and controls an LED on GPIO pin 18 (BCM numbering). The program polls the sensor inputs every 50 ms without using blocking delays. It handles GPIO initialization errors and cleans up all GPIO resources when receiving a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

