This C program reads the state of an 8-channel capacitive touch sensor (TTP226) connected to a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ via GPIO pins. It logs changes in touch state to the console with an ISO-8601 timestamp, sensor index, BCM GPIO number, and whether a touch was detected or released. The program includes robust error handling for GPIO chip initialization, line resolution, bulk line requests, and read failures. It ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including graceful shutdown on SIGINT (Ctrl-C). The program compiles cleanly with `gcc -Wall -Wextra -lgpiod`.

