This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B continuously monitors a KY-026 Flame Sensor connected to GPIO4 (BCM) and drives an alert output on GPIO17 (BCM). It polls the sensor every 500 ms, records each reading to an append-mode file named `fire_events.log` with a timestamp, and sets the alert pin HIGH for exactly 1 second when the sensor reports a flame. The program handles errors, performs signal-safe cleanup on termination, and ensures all resources are released on every exit path.

