This code implements a flame detection safety system using the Keyes KY-026 Flame Sensor and an active buzzer on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It polls the sensor every 500 ms, breaks the 2-second buzzer activation into 100 ms slices, and logs a timestamped "FLAME DETECTED" entry to a file named `alert_log.txt` on each HIGH-to-LOW transition. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to turn off the buzzer, release the GPIO lines, close the chip and log file, and exit cleanly.

