This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO bus. It reads the SainSmart TTP223B capacitive touch sensor connected to GPIO4 and toggles an LED connected to GPIO17. The program polls the touch sensor every 10 ms, detects a LOW-to-HIGH transition (rising edge), applies a 200 ms software debounce, and logs a UTC ISO-8601 timestamp to a file named `touch_log.txt` on each valid toggle event. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by turning off the LED, closing the log file, and calling the library's cleanup API before exiting.

