This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 5. It polls four KY-033 4-Way Infrared Tracking Module sensors connected to GPIO17, GPIO18, GPIO27, and GPIO22 every 100 ms. The program reads the active-low outputs of the sensors and appends a row to a timestamped CSV file named `tracking_log.csv`. The CSV file includes columns for timestamp and sensor readings. The program handles initialization errors, continues running even if a GPIO request or read fails, and performs a graceful shutdown on receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM signals, releasing all GPIO resources and closing the CSV file.

