This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It polls three Keywish 3-Way Tracking Sensor lines (GPIO2, GPIO3, and GPIO4) every 100 ms, reads their digital values, and logs them to stdout in the format "L:<0|1> M:<0|1> R:<0|1>". The program includes error handling for device absence, permission issues, and other errors. It also ensures that all resources are cleanly released on exit by installing a SIGINT handler that terminates the program gracefully.

