This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B communicates with a TCS34725 color sensor using the I2C bus and controls an LED connected to GPIO 17. It initializes the I2C bus, sets up the TCS34725 sensor, and enters a loop to read and print the calibrated red, green, blue, and clear values. The LED is turned on when the red value exceeds a threshold of 200 and off otherwise. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to clean up resources and exit gracefully.

