This C program reads the ambient light from a BH1750 digital light sensor on the I2C bus, stores the last 60 lux readings in a circular buffer, computes the average lux, and blinks an LED connected to GPIO17 with a frequency that varies from 0.5 Hz to 5 Hz based on the lux level. It handles errors, cleans up resources on program termination, and uses the libgpiod library for GPIO control.

