This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to control an LED and a button on a Raspberry Pi. It sets up GPIO24 as an output and GPIO22 as an input with a pull-down resistor. The program continuously monitors the button state. When the button is pressed, the LED blinks with a 500ms on/500ms off pattern. The LED turns off immediately when the button is released and remains off until the next press. The program handles errors and releases all resources on exit, including receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM.

