This code sets up a common-cathode RGB LED connected to GPIO24, GPIO23, and GPIO18 on a Raspberry Pi 5. It uses software PWM with a 100 Hz frequency and random intensity values for each color. The program runs indefinitely until the user presses Ctrl+C, at which point it cleans up and exits.

