This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W continuously polls an Adafruit LSM303DLHC accelerometer on I2C bus 1 at 10 Hz, computes the total G-force magnitude, and triggers an impact interrupt by setting GPIO17 (BCM numbering) as an output and pulsing it HIGH for 50 ms when the magnitude exceeds a configurable threshold. It logs the timestamped accelerometer data to a file named `impact_log.txt`. The program handles errors, checks the result of every I2C read and write operation, and ensures that all resources are released on any exit path.

