This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W uses the libgpiod library to communicate with the TDK InvenSense ICM-20602 IMU over I2C bus 1. It performs burst reads of the six accelerometer bytes and six gyroscope bytes at a 10 Hz rate (every 100 ms), checks the return value of every I2C operation, prints any failures to stderr, timestamps each sample, and appends the x, y, z accelerometer and gyroscope values to a file named `imu_log.csv`. The program handles Ctrl+C (SIGINT) gracefully by closing the I2C handle, terminating the driver library, and closing the CSV file before exiting.

