This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B uses the SparkFun ADXL345 I2C accelerometer to detect free-fall events via a GPIO interrupt. It verifies the device ID at startup, places the sensor in standby mode, and captures timestamped acceleration samples (X, Y, Z) only while free-fall is active, writing them to a file named `freefall_log.csv`. The program checks every I2C system call and GPIO operation for errors, handles sensor-absent and bus-error conditions, runs a poll-based loop on the driver's event file descriptor, and cleans up resources on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM.

