This C program reads acceleration data from an Omron D7S-0001 vibration sensor over the I2C bus `/dev/i2c-1`, samples the X, Y, and Z axes every 100 ms, and appends each sample to a file named `vibration_log.csv` with a header line "Timestamp,X,Y,Z". The program checks the result of every open, ioctl, and read call, detects the documented sensor-absent condition, handles any bus errors gracefully, and on a read failure prints a diagnostic message to stderr and simply skips that sample. A SIGINT handler is installed so that pressing Ctrl+C cleanly closes the I2C file descriptor and the CSV file before the program exits.

