This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B continuously monitors two TI DRV5032 digital Hall-Effect sensors connected to the GPIO bus. It logs the millisecond-precision timestamped state of each sensor to a file named `conveyor_log.txt` every 50 ms. When both sensors read logic 1, it simulates halting the conveyor by printing a halt message. The program includes robust error handling for all GPIO access operations and file I/O, and it handles `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` to perform a graceful shutdown that releases all driver resources cleanly on every exit path.

