This code implements a dual-factor door-lock authentication scheme using two UART ports and two active-HIGH relay modules on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads 6-digit codes from `/dev/serial0` and `/dev/serial1` at 9600 baud, 8N1 framing, with a 5-second per-port read timeout and non-blocking reads in a single main loop. The codes must match each other and the constant expected code "123456" (using a constant-time string comparison to avoid timing side-channels) to unlock the door. The program handles errors, logs to stderr, and performs a clean shutdown on SIGINT and SIGTERM.

