This C program initializes a 4-channel relay module connected to a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using the libgpiod library. It sets up a timer that triggers every 60 seconds to activate each relay for 5 minutes, followed by a 1-minute pause. The program logs every state change to syslog with timestamps and the identifier "irrigation_system". It handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by deactivating all relays, releasing GPIO resources, and exiting cleanly.

