This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ continuously reads the heading from an HMC5883L magnetometer on I2C bus 1, applies hard-iron compensation using the offsets X = 100 and Y = -50, stores each compensated heading in an in-memory circular buffer of 100 entries overwriting the oldest when full, samples at a 100 ms interval, and drives GPIO17 (BCM numbering) high whenever the compensated heading deviates by more than 10 degrees from the target heading of 90.0 degrees and low otherwise. The program handles I2C errors by logging the condition and retrying without crashing, and it cleanly releases all resources on every exit path, including proper handling of SIGINT and SIGTERM.

