This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to control a 28BYJ-48 unipolar stepper motor through an L293D H-bridge driver on a Raspberry Pi. It initializes the GPIO pins for the stepper motor and buttons, sets up signal handlers for graceful exit, and implements a full-step two-phase drive with a 2 ms inter-step delay. The program rotates the motor 512 steps clockwise on a LOCK press and 512 steps counter-clockwise on an UNLOCK press, providing console feedback for each event. It handles driver initialization failure, checks all GPIO configuration return codes, prevents re-triggering while a button remains held, and ensures that on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, the motor coils are cleanly de-energized and all driver resources are released.

