This code implements a rudimentary theremin using an HC-SR04 ultrasonic distance sensor and a PWM buzzer on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It uses the `libgpiod` library for GPIO control. The program reads the distance from the sensor, maps it to a frequency for the buzzer, and ensures a minimum measurement interval. It handles errors, logs failures to `stderr`, and cleans up resources on `SIGINT`.

