This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ continuously reads edge events from an SW-420 vibration sensor module, handles edge-triggered polling on both rising and falling edges, accepts an optional poll timeout in milliseconds, maintains a sliding window of the last five events, prints an "EARTHQUAKE ALERT" message when three or more events are HIGH, logs every edge event to a file, handles file open and write errors, checks library and system call return values, and installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler to exit cleanly.

