This code provides a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B that reads distance from an HC-SR04 ultrasonic distance sensor and logs the result every second to a file named `distance_log.txt`. It uses the `libgpiod` library for GPIO control and handles errors and resource cleanup properly. The program generates a 10 µs trigger pulse, waits for the rising and falling edges of the echo signal, computes the distance, and writes the value to the log file. It also includes signal handlers to cleanly release resources and close the log file on `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM`.

