This C program reads the angular velocity from an MPU-6050 gyroscope over the hardware I2C bus `/dev/i2c-1` using the documented device address. It continuously acquires the x, y, and z axis rotation rates and logs those three values to the console. The program checks the result of every I2C read and write system call and handles any sensor-absent or bus-error conditions gracefully. It also installs signal handlers for `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` so that all resources are cleanly released on any exit path.

