This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W reads angular rate data from an Analog Devices ADXRS290 dual-axis gyroscope over SPI channel 0 using CE0 on GPIO8 (BCM) at 1 MHz, mode 0 (CPOL = 0, CPHA = 0). It samples both axes at roughly 100 Hz with a 10 ms delay between samples and logs each sample to a file named `gyro_data.csv` containing a timestamp (seconds since epoch with microsecond precision), the raw X-axis rate as a signed 16-bit integer, and the raw Y-axis rate as a signed 16-bit integer. Each register read is performed by sending the register address OR'd with the documented read-bit followed by a dummy byte and taking the second byte of the transfer as the response. The program performs proper error checking on all SPI and GPIO calls and on file operations, and if a read fails, it attempts to re-initialize the SPI interface up to three times before exiting. A signal handler for SIGINT (Ctrl-C) cleans up the SPI device, flushes and closes the CSV file, terminates the driver usage, and releases all resources (SPI handle, file, driver) on every exit path.

