This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W implements a smart sunset simulator for three relay-controlled dimmable lamps connected to GPIO17, GPIO18, and GPIO27. It validates the user-defined total duration, initializes the hardware PWM driver library, uses hardware PWM at 100 Hz with a duty-cycle range of 0-255, emits status messages, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM gracefully.

