This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ continuously monitors a TTP223 capacitive touch sensor connected to GPIO4 and toggles a 5V relay attached to GPIO17 each time a touch is detected. The program uses the libgpiod library for GPIO operations, handles errors gracefully, and ensures proper cleanup on exit. It also includes robust signal handling to gracefully terminate the program with Ctrl-C.

