This C program for a Raspberry Pi 5 continuously reads the Adafruit LIS3DH accelerometer on I2C bus 1, detects a free-fall when the measured acceleration magnitude falls below 0.2 g, and detects an impact when the magnitude rises above 1.5 g. It activates a buzzer connected to GPIO17 (BCM) for exactly one second upon detecting the impact. The program includes full error checking, retries for I2C communication failures, graceful handling of sensor or bus errors, and a clean shutdown on receipt of SIGINT.

