This code provides a basic framework for an autonomous line-following robot using a SunFounder 3-Way Tracking Sensor on a Raspberry Pi 5. It initializes the GPIO lines, polls the sensors every 10 ms, logs the sensor readings into a circular buffer, and controls the robot based on the sensor readings. The robot turns left, right, or moves forward based on the sensor inputs. It also handles the alert pin to indicate when the robot is not on a line for five consecutive readings. The program ensures that all resources are released cleanly on exit paths triggered by SIGINT or SIGTERM.

