This C program for a Raspberry Pi 5 continuously monitors the Seeed Studio Rain Sensor v1.0 digital output on GPIO 17 (BCM) configured as an input with a pull-up, polling every 200 ms over the GPIO bus. It drives a DC motor window actuator through an L298N driver using ENA on GPIO 22 (BCM), IN1 on GPIO 23 (BCM), and IN2 on GPIO 24 (BCM). The program detects a rising-edge (dry-to-wet transition) and, on that edge only, starts the close-window sequence by setting ENA high, IN1 high, IN2 low, holding the motor for exactly 5 seconds, then stopping the motor by setting ENA low and both IN1 and IN2 low. It logs all events with syslog and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to perform a graceful shutdown.

