This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ continuously monitors weight using a TAL220B load cell with an HX711 amplifier over a bit-banged GPIO bus. It reads the HX711 DOUT on GPIO23 and HX711 SCK on GPIO24, and drives a solenoid lock on GPIO25. The program performs a startup tare by averaging ten 24-bit two's-complement readings, then in the main loop polls the weight every 500 ms, averaging five readings per measurement cycle, applies an optional scale factor, and if the measured weight exceeds a threshold activates the solenoid lock by setting GPIO25 HIGH for 200 ms before returning it LOW. Each HX711 read checks that DOUT goes LOW within 1 second, logging an error via syslog and retrying up to three times before exiting. The program accepts optional `--scale <factor>` and `--duration <ms>` arguments, logs informational and error messages through syslog, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM performs a graceful shutdown that releases all GPIO lines and chips, closes syslog, and ensures the solenoid is set LOW before exiting.

