This code provides a complete implementation of closed-loop DC motor speed control for a miniature vehicle using quadrature encoders, driving two DC motors through a DRV8833 H-bridge on the GPIO bus with PWM and digital signals. It uses the libgpiod library for GPIO operations and handles errors and resource management properly. The program runs a PI control loop every 100 ms with a 10 kHz PWM frequency, targets 50 RPM for both motors, and includes anti-windup clamping in the controller. It also detects encoder stalls and prints warnings when detected. The program handles SIGINT by stopping the motors and releasing all resources cleanly.

