This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B continuously monitors a kitchen ingredient stock level using a TAL220B load cell amplified by an HX711 connected on the GPIO bus with bit-banged communication. It reads the data line (DT) on GPIO23 (BCM) and the clock line (SCK) on GPIO24 (BCM), checks the weight once every second, and activates a solenoid lock attached to GPIO17 (BCM) for exactly five seconds when the measured weight falls below 100 grams. The program logs each weight check, lock activation, and any error condition to a file named `stock_events.txt`, and it implements robust error handling for all reads, writes, and file operations. The program performs proper resource cleanup when receiving `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM`.

