This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ implements a timed watering system by activating a Parker Hannifin Series 9 General Purpose Miniature Solenoid Valve through an external N-channel MOSFET or relay module connected to GPIO18 (BCM) on the GPIO bus. The program reads the watering duration from a configuration file named `watering.conf`, initializes the GPIO line as an output with active-low = 0 and a default low value (valve off), activates the valve by setting the line high, waits the configured duration using a signal-safe interruptible sleep, then sets the line low, prints status messages to stdout showing the configured duration and each valve on/off transition, performs error handling by checking every driver call for errors and printing descriptive messages to stderr, installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler that sets a volatile sig_atomic_t flag, has the main loop poll this flag and turn the valve off before exiting, and ensures that on every exit path—whether normal completion, signal receipt, or error—the GPIO line is released and the chip closed so the valve is always left off.

