This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ uses the libgpiod library to handle GPIO input from an IR receiver (TSOP38238) connected to GPIO17 (BCM). It captures pulse timings on the falling edge of the GPIO, decodes NEC infrared remote signals, and reports the decoded commands both to syslog and to an MQTT broker at localhost on port 1883 using the topic `ir/decoded`. The program includes error handling, resource management, and signal handling to ensure clean shutdown.

