This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W opens the I2C bus `/dev/i2c-1`, issues a zero-length I2C write to generate a start condition, reads two bytes from the Honeywell AWM7300V mass airflow sensor, masks the 14-bit flow value, converts it to SLPM, and logs a timestamped flow-rate entry to a file named `airflow_log.txt` once per second. It handles retries for transient I2C read failures, checks for distinct error paths for a missing sensor (ENXIO) and a bus error (EIO), and installs a SIGINT handler to cleanly close the I2C file descriptor and flush and close the log file before exiting.

