This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W reads tri-axial acceleration data from an Omron D7S seismic sensor over the I2C bus and logs the timestamped X, Y, Z values in g to a CSV file named `seismic_data.csv` by default. It also writes any error messages with timestamps to `seismic_error.log`. The program accepts command-line options `-a` to specify the I2C address, `-i` to set the sampling interval in seconds, and `-f` to set the output filename. It performs reads at the configured interval, checks every I2C read/write return value, retries transient failures up to three times with a 10 ms backoff, detects sensor-absent and bus-error conditions, and handles `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` to gracefully shut down by closing the I2C file descriptor and flushing and closing the CSV file on all exit paths.

